  "summary": "The code suffered from critical performance bottlenecks due to per-request environment instantiation and a high-severity XSS vulnerability. I have refactored the Jinja2 environment to be global, enabled autoescaping, added type hints, and implemented input length limiting to improve overall security and maintainability.",
  "fixed_code": "import os\nfrom flask import Flask, request\nfrom jinja2 import Environment, FileSystemLoader, select_autoescape\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n# Initialize environment globally with autoescape enabled for security\nenv = Environment(\n    loader=FileSystemLoader(os.path.join(app.root_path, 'templates')),\n    autoescape=select_autoescape(['html', 'xml'])\n)\n\n@app.route('/render')\ndef render_response_from_env() -> str:\n    '''\n    Get the argument \"name\" from request, \n    render template.html using the global environment.\n    '''\n    # Limit input length to prevent potential resource exhaustion\n    name = request.args.get('name', '')[:100]\n    template = env.get_template('template.html')\n    return template.render(name=name)"
